{
  "id": "geo-similarity",
  "chapterNumber": "4",
  "title": {
    "en": "Similarity",
    "ar": null
  },
  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Similar figures have the same shape but not necessarily the same size: equal angles and sides in a constant ratio. The ratio — the <strong>scale factor</strong> — governs lengths, areas and volumes differently.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Definition 4.1 — Similar polygons",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Two polygons are <strong>similar</strong> when corresponding angles are equal and corresponding sides are in proportion. Triangles need only two equal angles (<strong>AA</strong>) to be similar.</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Side ratio",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\dfrac{a'}{a}=k \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Perimeter ratio",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "k",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Area ratio",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( k^{2} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Triangle test",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "AA similarity",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 4.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>A \\( 6 \\)-ft person casts a \\( 4 \\)-ft shadow while a tree casts a \\( 20 \\)-ft shadow. Find the tree's height.</p><p>Similar triangles give \\( \\dfrac{6}{4}=\\dfrac{h}{20} \\):</p>\\[ h=\\frac{6\\times 20}{4}=30\\ \\text{ft}. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 4.B",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Two similar figures have side ratio \\( 1:3 \\). What is the ratio of their areas?</p>\\[ 1^{2}:3^{2}=1:9. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
